course: dictionary
lesson: 2764
title: Taking a word apart
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The prefix «dis-» at the start of a word often means apart, not, or the opposite. Connect means join, so disconnect means to separate things that were joined.
explain: «Games usually still count a match as lost if a player disconnects or quits.» A player who disconnects is cut off from the game, like quitting. Test it: swap in "gets cut off" and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Disconnect can also be a noun. «A disconnect between what he says and what he does» means his words and actions do not match up, so the two parts are not joined.
fact: Disconnect means to separate two things that were joined, such as a plug from a socket.
fact: «Disconnect the power» means switch off the electricity, so a device is safe to clean or fix.
fact: A phone call or internet connection can disconnect, which means it is cut off.
fact: «Disconnect from screens» means take a break from phones and games to rest.
fact: «A disconnect» (noun) means a lack of connection or understanding between people or ideas.
exercise: «Games usually still count a match as lost if a player disconnects or quits.» What does disconnects mean here? | Plays very slowly | Wins the match | Makes a new friend | *Gets cut off from the game
exercise: Before you clean a device, you must «disconnect the power». Why? | To make the screen brighter | *To switch off the electricity so it is safe | To make the device faster | To charge the battery
exercise: Mum says, «Let's disconnect from screens for an hour.» What does she mean? | Connect the screen to the TV | Make the screen louder | *Take a rest from screens | Buy a bigger screen
test: In «a disconnect between what he says and what he does», what is the disconnect? | *A lack of match between his words and his actions | A wire that is joined tightly | A happy ending | A very fast car
test: When a phone call drops, the call is disconnected. What does disconnected mean? | Joined together | Much louder | *Cut off | Finished with a prize
exam: Which sentence uses disconnect to mean separate things that were joined? | The kettle was loud and hot. | *Please disconnect the kettle from the wall before you clean it. | Please connect the printer to the computer. | The two friends had a disconnect after the game.
